{"unit":7,"items":54,"pass":38,"title":"Unit Test · Unit 7","tracks":{"a71":"Track_7.1.mp3"},"SEGS":{"prog":["a71",3.84,null]},"html":"\n  <section class=\"stage on\" data-stage=\"Unit Test\">\n    <div class=\"stage-head\">\n      <div class=\"kicker\">Unit 7 &middot; Unit Test</div>\n      <h2>Work and ambition</h2>\n      <p>Six parts, <b>54 questions</b>, covering everything in Unit 7, with four questions that come back from Units 1&ndash;6. Answer them all, then press Check. You need <b>38 out of 54</b> to pass. Parts 7 and 8 are your writing and speaking &mdash; they are not marked automatically, but do not skip them. You can take this test as many times as you like.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"task\" data-task data-tid=\"review-u7\">\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 1 · VOCABULARY ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\">Part 1 &middot; Vocabulary &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 1&ndash;12</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the word that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">1</span><span class=\"body\">The contract is only for six months, so the post is&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">rent-free</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">unskilled</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">temporary</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">2</span><span class=\"body\">She left without another job to go to &mdash; she simply&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">quit</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">obeyed</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">retrained</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">3</span><span class=\"body\">Two hundred people applied, and every&hellip; was interviewed by phone first.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">executive</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">applicant</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">specialist</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">4</span><span class=\"body\">The factory closed and four hundred people were made&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">ambitious</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">determined</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">redundant</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Match the two halves of each phrase. Click one on the left, then one on the right.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">5&ndash;9</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"pairbox\">\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"k1\">make</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"k2\">get to</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"k3\">working</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"k4\">a point of</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"k5\">up to</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"k3\" data-short=\"conditions\">conditions</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"k5\" data-short=\"date\">date</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"k1\" data-short=\"progress\">progress</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"k4\" data-short=\"view\">view</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"k2\" data-short=\"the top\">the top</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the word formed from the word in brackets.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">10</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>ambition</i>) She is the most <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"ambitious\" data-why=\"<b>Ambition</b> &rarr; the adjective <b>ambitious</b>.\"> person on the team.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">11</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>manage</i>) The advertisement asks for four years of <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"management\" data-why=\"<b>Manage</b> &rarr; the noun <b>management</b>.\"> experience.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">12</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>fail</i>) He talks about that year as his one great <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"failure\" data-why=\"<b>Fail</b> &rarr; the noun <b>failure</b>.\"> .</span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 2 · GRAMMAR ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 2 &middot; Grammar &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 13&ndash;26</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the correct form. Sometimes only one is possible.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">13</span><span class=\"body\">There&hellip; a factory on this corner, but they knocked it down.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">would be</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">used to be</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">was using to be</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">14</span><span class=\"body\">Every Friday we&hellip; at four and go straight to the river.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">used to finishing</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">are used to finish</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">would finish</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">15</span><span class=\"body\">&hellip; you use to work nights when you started?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">Did</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">Would</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Used</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">16</span><span class=\"body\">Getting up at five is normal for me now. I&hellip; it.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">used to</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">am used to</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">would</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the question for the underlined part of the answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">17</span><span class=\"body\"><u>Her sister</u> persuaded her to apply.<br><input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"who persuaded her to apply\" data-why=\"The answer is the subject, so there is no <i>did</i>.\"> ?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">18</span><span class=\"body\">She studied <u>anthropology</u>.<br><input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"what did she study\" data-why=\"The answer is the object, so the question needs <b>did</b> + base verb.\"> ?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">19</span><span class=\"body\">She has worked there <u>for eleven years</u>.<br><input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"how long has she worked there\" data-why=\"Present perfect question: <b>has</b> before the subject.\"> ?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">20</span><span class=\"body\">They interviewed <u>forty applicants</u>.<br><input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"how many applicants did they interview\" data-why=\"The answer is the object &rarr; <b>did</b> + base verb.\"> ?</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each question with the missing auxiliary, or write <b>nothing</b> if none is needed.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">21</span><span class=\"body\">Who <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"nothing|none|no auxiliary\" data-why=\"A subject question needs no auxiliary: <i>Who taught you?</i>\"> taught you to do that?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">22</span><span class=\"body\">What <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"does\" data-why=\"Present simple, third person, object question &rarr; <b>does</b>.\"> a decision maker actually do all day?</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">23</span><span class=\"body\">He <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"didn’t use to|did not use to\" data-why=\"The negative is <b>didn&rsquo;t use to</b> &mdash; no <i>-d</i> after <i>did</i>.\"> work at that branch.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">24</span><span class=\"body\">He asked me what <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"she studied\" data-why=\"A reported question keeps statement order and drops <i>did</i>: <b>what she studied</b>.\"> at university.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the second sentence so that it means the same as the first.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">25</span><span class=\"body\">I worked nights for two years, but I do not now.<br>I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"used to work nights\" data-why=\"A past habit that has stopped &rarr; <b>used to</b>.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">26</span><span class=\"body\">Ask politely how many people she supervises.<br>Could I ask <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"how many people you supervise|how many people she supervises\" data-why=\"After <i>Could I ask</i>, statement order and no <b>do</b>.\"> ?</span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 3 · READING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 3 &middot; Reading &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 27&ndash;34</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the whole text once before you answer anything.</p>\n\n      <article class=\"reading\">\n        <h3>The job that reappeared</h3>\n        <p class=\"stand\">Everybody expects machines to remove work. Sometimes a machine removes a job and then, quietly, puts a version of it back.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">A</span>When the first cash machines arrived in the 1970s, the prediction was obvious: banks would need far fewer people behind the counter. The first half of that came true. A branch that used to need twenty staff could be run by thirteen. What nobody predicted was the second half. Because branches were cheaper to run, banks opened many more of them, and the total number of people employed as cashiers in the United States rose for the next thirty years.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">B</span>The work itself changed completely. The old job was counting; the new one was selling and explaining. Staff who used to spend the day handling notes were retrained to open accounts, arrange loans and deal with the customers a machine could not. Some of them found the new job better. Others said they had not applied to be salespeople and would have preferred the counter.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">C</span>Economists who study this call it the difference between a task and an occupation. Machines take tasks. Occupations are bundles of tasks, and when one is removed the bundle is re-tied, usually around whatever the machine still cannot do. That is why the disappearance of a task so rarely produces the clean unemployment that headlines promise.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">D</span>None of which means the change was painless. The retraining was real work, and it fell hardest on people who had been doing the old job longest. The comfortable version of this story &mdash; technology destroys jobs, technology creates better ones &mdash; skips the years in between, and it is those years that people actually have to live through. What the cash machine really shows is not that nothing is lost. It is that what is lost and what appears are almost never the same thing, and almost never happen to the same person at the same time.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">27</span><span class=\"body\">Why did the number of bank cashiers rise?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">the machines broke down often</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">cheaper branches meant banks opened many more of them</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">customers refused to use the machines</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">28</span><span class=\"body\">How did the cashier&rsquo;s job change?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">it became better paid but shorter</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">it stayed the same but with fewer hours</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">it moved from counting money to selling and explaining</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">True, False, or Not given? Choose for each sentence.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">29</span><span class=\"body\">A branch that once needed twenty staff could be run by thirteen. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph A gives exactly those numbers.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">30</span><span class=\"body\">All the retrained staff preferred the new job. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph B: others would have preferred the counter.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"T\">True</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">31</span><span class=\"body\">Cashiers were paid more after the retraining. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"Pay is never mentioned.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">32</span><span class=\"body\">The writer thinks the change caused no difficulty at all. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph D: it fell hardest on those who had done the old job longest.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Answer the last two questions about the whole text.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">33</span><span class=\"body\">In paragraph C, <i>the bundle is re-tied</i> means that\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">the remaining tasks are grouped into a new version of the job</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">the job disappears completely</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">workers are given two jobs instead of one</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">34</span><span class=\"body\">The writer&rsquo;s main criticism of the comfortable version of the story is that it\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">exaggerates how many jobs were lost</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">ignores the years people have to live through in between</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">was invented by economists</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 4 · LISTENING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 4 &middot; Listening &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 35&ndash;40</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the questions first. Then play the recording twice.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('prog',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Three people who left\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 7.1</b>Original coursebook recording</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the notes with one word.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">35</span><span class=\"body\">Before she moved, Maria had been out of work in Athens for over a <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"year\" data-why=\"She had been unemployed for over a <b>year</b>.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">36</span><span class=\"body\">Maria has retrained as a landscape <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"designer\" data-why=\"She retrained as a landscape <b>designer</b>.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">37</span><span class=\"body\">Joaquim says that living in Luanda is extremely <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"expensive\" data-why=\"He says the city is extremely <b>expensive</b>.\"> .</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">38</span><span class=\"body\">Maria says she used to spend all day ringing people up and &ldquo;getting nowhere&rdquo;. She means\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">she could not afford the phone calls</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">she did not know who to call</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">none of the calls produced a job</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">39</span><span class=\"body\">Joaquim says the job is temporary, &ldquo;but now I&rsquo;m here I think I&rsquo;ll stay a lot longer&rdquo;. This suggests he\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">has changed his mind since arriving</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">has been offered a permanent contract</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">regrets moving</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">40</span><span class=\"body\">The interviewer&rsquo;s purpose is to find out\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">which country pays best</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">why they moved and how it worked out</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">how to get a visa</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 5 · FUNCTIONAL LANGUAGE ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 5 &middot; Functional language &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 41&ndash;48</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the version you would actually use with a manager.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">41</span><span class=\"body\"><select data-answer=\"Could you tell me what the procedure is?\" data-why=\"After <i>Could you tell me what the procedure is?</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>What is the procedure?</option><option>Could you tell me what is the procedure?</option><option>Could you tell me what the procedure is?</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">42</span><span class=\"body\"><select data-answer=\"Sorry, could you explain what you mean by that?\" data-why=\"The standard polite request for a definition.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>Sorry, could you explain what you mean by that?</option><option>What? Say it again.</option><option>In other words, that.</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">43</span><span class=\"body\"><select data-answer=\"Would you mind explaining what that means here?\" data-why=\"<b>Would you mind explaining what that means here?</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>Would you mind to explain what means that here?</option><option>Would you mind explaining what that means here?</option><option>What means that here?</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Where does each line belong?</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">44&ndash;47</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"sortbox\">\n          <div class=\"sortpool\"><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Letter\">I am writing to apply for the position of Assistant Manager.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Chat\">I&rsquo;d love this job, it looks amazing!</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Letter\">I would be glad to discuss my application at any time that suits you.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Chat\">Give me a shout if you want a chat.</button></div>\n          <div class=\"sortcols\"><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Letter\"><h5>The application letter</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Chat\"><h5>Too informal for it</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div></div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the four parts of the application letter in order.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">48</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"order\" data-order=\"a2,a4,a1,a3\">\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"a1\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">I believe I would be well suited to this position for two reasons.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"a2\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">I am writing to apply for the position advertised on your website on 2 March.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"a3\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">Please find attached an up to date copy of my CV. Yours sincerely, Amina Serikova</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"a4\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">I have worked in customer service for four years, the last two as a team leader.</span></button>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 6 · PUTTING IT TOGETHER ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 6 &middot; Putting it together &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 49&ndash;54</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the interview. Two of these gaps come back from earlier units. <span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span></p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"chat\">\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Interviewer</b><select data-answer=\"What made you apply\" data-why=\"A subject question &mdash; <i>What made you apply</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>What did make you apply</option><option>What you made apply</option><option>What made you apply</option></select> for this position?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>A friend pushed me into it. I <select data-answer=\"used to be\" data-why=\"A past state that has ended &rarr; <b>used to be</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>used to be</option><option>would be</option><option>am used to be</option></select> quite happy where I was.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Interviewer</b>And what <select data-answer=\"did you do\" data-why=\"An object question &rarr; <b>did you do</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>you did</option><option>did you do</option><option>did you did</option></select> there, exactly?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Customer service. Every Friday we <select data-answer=\"would close\" data-why=\"A repeated past action &rarr; <b>would close</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>used to closing</option><option>would close</option><option>are used to close</option></select> the branch together and count everything by hand.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Interviewer</b>The role here involves a flexible reporting line.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b><select data-answer=\"Sorry, could you explain\" data-why=\"A polite request for a definition.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>Sorry, could you explain</option><option>What? Say again</option><option>In other words</option></select> what you mean by that? <span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span> And could you tell me <select data-answer=\"whether the season dates are fixed\" data-why=\"An indirect yes/no question &rarr; <b>whether the season dates are fixed</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>are the season dates fixed</option><option>whether are the season dates fixed</option><option>whether the season dates are fixed</option></select>?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Interviewer</b>June to September, every year.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Thank you. So, if I understand you correctly, I would report to two people for four months of the year.</div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" onclick=\"checkReview(this)\" style=\"margin-top:24px\">Check my answers</button>\n      <div class=\"res\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"reviewResult\" class=\"review-result\"></div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 7 · WRITING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Part 7 &middot; Writing &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">Write 120&ndash;140 words. Give yourself twenty-five minutes.</p>\n    <div class=\"opentask\" data-open data-tid=\"test-write\">\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <p class=\"ohint\"><b>The task.</b> Write a letter of application for a job you would actually like. Name the position and where you saw it. Say what you have done, with <b>one number</b> that proves something. Give two reasons why you would suit the role. Say what you want next and why this company. Point to your CV and offer to meet. Do not list every job you have ever had.</p>\n        <textarea placeholder=\"Dear&hellip;   I am writing to apply for the position of&hellip;   I have worked in&hellip; for&hellip;   I believe I would be well suited&hellip;   Please find attached&hellip;   Yours sincerely,\" data-track></textarea>\n      </span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bubble useful\">\n      <div class=\"blab\">Your letter must contain</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>the position and where you saw it, in the <b>first</b> sentence</li>\n        <li>exactly one number that proves something real</li>\n        <li>two reasons, marked <b>First&hellip; Second&hellip;</b></li>\n        <li>the matching pair: a name &rarr; <b>Yours sincerely</b>, no name &rarr; <b>Yours faithfully</b></li>\n        <li>one <b>used to</b> or <b>would</b> about what you did before</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 8 · SPEAKING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 8 &middot; Speaking &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <div class=\"opentask speak\" data-open data-tid=\"test-speak\">\n      <div class=\"sp-head\"><span class=\"sp-ic\">&#127908;</span>\n        <div><b>Speaking &mdash; then and now, and six questions</b><span>Extended turn</span></div></div>\n      <p class=\"sp-task\"><b>Part A.</b> Describe how work or study used to be for you or your family, and how it is now. Ninety seconds. <b>Part B.</b> Then interview an imaginary expert about their career: ask six questions out loud, including at least two subject questions and one softened question.</p>\n      <ul class=\"sp-list\">\n        <li><b>used to</b> for states, <b>would</b> for repeated actions, past simple for single events</li>\n        <li>at least two subject questions with no <i>do</i> or <i>did</i> in them</li>\n        <li>one question wrapped in <i>Could you tell me&hellip;</i> with the word order back to normal</li>\n        <li>one request for clarification, as though you had not understood</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"sp-lang\"><b>Use this language</b>We used to&hellip; &middot; Every Friday we would&hellip; &middot; Who taught you&hellip;? &middot; What made you&hellip;? &middot; Could you tell me whether&hellip; &middot; Sorry, could you explain what you mean by&hellip;?</div>\n      <div class=\"rec\">\n        <div class=\"rec-row\">\n          <button class=\"rec-btn\" type=\"button\" onclick=\"recToggle(this)\" aria-label=\"Record your answer\" title=\"Record\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M12 14a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V6a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v5a3 3 0 0 0 3 3zm5-3a5 5 0 0 1-10 0H5a7 7 0 0 0 6 6.9V21h2v-3.1A7 7 0 0 0 19 11z\"/></svg></button>\n          <div class=\"rec-label\"><b>Record your answer</b><span>Press the microphone and speak</span></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-wave\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-time\">0:00</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"rec-takes\"></div>\n        <div class=\"rec-note\">Record it, play it back, then submit it for assessment.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Parts 7 and 8 &middot; Assessment</div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">These two parts are not marked automatically and they are not marked by you. Submit your writing and record your speaking, then your teacher &mdash; or the AI tutor &mdash; scores each part against the criteria below and writes the feedback.</p>\n    <div class=\"rubric-slot\">\n      <ul class=\"reqlist\">\n        <li>my first sentence names the position and where I saw it</li>\n        <li>I gave one number that proves something, not a list of duties</li>\n        <li>my two reasons are marked, so the reader can count them</li>\n        <li>my opening and my sign-off match each other</li>\n        <li>I used <i>used to</i> for a state and <i>would</i> for a repeated action</li>\n        <li>no state verb of mine went with <i>would</i></li>\n        <li>my subject questions had no <i>do</i> or <i>did</i> in them</li>\n        <li>after <i>Could you tell me&hellip;</i> I used statement word order</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n"}